Non-blocking: This can be simplified a bit by defining a closure like so:

```rust
let array_from_table = |table: &Table, key: &str| table.get(key).unwrap().as_array().unwrap();
```

This way you got:

```rust
array_from_table(features, "default").iter().flat_map(|v| {
  std::iter::once(v.as_str().unwrap().to_string()).chain(
    array_from_table(features, v.as_str().unwrap())
      .iter()
      .map(|v| v.as_str().unwrap().to_string()),
  )
})
```
Also I believe it's possible to `default: Vec<&toml::value::Value>`, since `Value` implements `PartialEq<Value>` it can be compared still.

```rust
array_from_table(features, "default").iter().flat_map(|v| {
  std::iter::once(v).chain(
    array_from_table(features, v.as_str().unwrap()).iter()
  )
})
```

